# Generated-project secret-scan allowlist.
#
# Three entry forms (ops/release/secret-scan.mjs, matchesAllowList):
#   <exact value>              suppress this exact value anywhere, ENTROPY/SECRET-ASSIGNMENT ONLY
#   path:<glob>#<exact value>  suppress this exact token only inside matching files
#   path:<glob>                suppress ONLY the two heuristic detectors (entropy,
#                              secret-assignment) inside matching files
#
# R3-07: a bare `path:` entry does NOT exempt a file from every detector. A real AWS key, Stripe
# key, GitHub/GitLab token, package token, private key or JWT planted in an allowlisted fixture file
# is still reported unless that exact value is listed. Prefer the scoped
# `path:<glob>#<exact value>` form over a whole-file entry.
#
# R5-06: a bare value entry reaches the two heuristic detectors ONLY, and THIS FILE IS SCANNED by
# the secret_scan gate. A credential written here - as a bare entry, in a comment, anywhere - is
# reported; only the exact values declared in the scoped `path:<glob>#<value>` form are suppressed
# inside this file.
#
# Never add a real secret here. A real credential belongs in the secret store, not in the repository.
